 clean←Requote text;t;exeme
⍝ APL+Win allows two kinds of character quotation marks (' & ") while Dyalog allows only one (').
⍝ This function is used during run-time to convert APL+Win-style executable strings into Dyalog-style.
⍝ It is normally called to pre-process arguments to the Execute (⍎) primitive or equivalent implied execution.
⍝ It also adds a recursive call to itself to any imbedded ⍎ primitives within the expression.
⍝ If the configuration is set for auto-migration translation, process that on the executable-code portion of as well.

⍝ A simplified quote-replacement function from Morten, but it does not avoid comments or handle imbedded executes:
⍝       '''[^'']*''' '"[^"]*"'⎕R{⍵.('\"' ''''⎕R'''' ''''''⍣PatternNum⊢Match)}

 exeme←'⍎',⊃⎕XSI ⍝ Executable recursive execution text (may substitute an execute-replacement function for ⍎ if necessary)
 :If ∧/'⍎'∊¨exeme text ⋄ exeme←GUIroot._Translate exeme ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Automatically translate any remaining ⍎ if available
 clean←0⍴text←,text ⍝ We'll have to build this piecemeal, I think, to avoid really difficult ⎕R-work
 :While ×≢text
     clean,←GUIroot._Translate(t←¯1+⌊/text⍳'''"⍝⍎')↑text ⍝ Grab all the text preceding any signal characters and translate as specified
     :Select ⊃text←t↓text ⍝ Handle each signal character differently, one at a time
     :Case '''' ⋄ clean,←(t←+/∧\≠\⍛∨⊃⍛=text)↑text ⋄ text↓⍨←t
     :Case '"' ⋄ clean,←'\"' ''''⎕R'''' ''''''⊢(t←+/∧\≠\⍛∨⊃⍛=text)↑text ⋄ text↓⍨←t
     :Case '⍝' ⋄ clean,←text ⋄ text←''
     :Case '⍎' ⋄ clean,←exeme,' ' ⋄ text↓⍨←1
     :EndSelect
 :EndWhile
